{
  "name": "Generate PDF certificates from Google Sheets and email them with Gmail",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "1e0b04e7-00ba-41ed-a93a-18888cec85a6",
      "name": "Template description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -700,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Generate PDF certificates from Google Sheets and email them with Gmail\n\n### Who's it for\nSchools, online course creators, training companies, coding clubs, event organizers and HR teams who hand out certificates or diplomas to many people at once.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Read participants** loads your list from Google Sheets (one row per person).\n2. **Build Actor input** turns the rows into the input for the **Bulk Certificate & Diploma PDF Generator** on Apify, using the text and design from **Settings**.\n3. **Generate PDFs on Apify** creates one print-ready PDF per person (unique certificate ID, full Unicode incl. diacritics and Cyrillic).\n4. **Match emails** links every PDF back to the person's email.\n5. **Download PDF** and **Email certificate** send each person their own PDF as an attachment.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Sheet columns: `name`, `email`, plus any column you want in the text (`course`, `date`, `hours`...).\n2. Connect Google Sheets and Gmail.\n3. Create a **Header Auth** credential named `Apify API token`: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN` (Apify Console \u2192 Settings \u2192 API & Integrations). Select it in both HTTP nodes.\n4. Edit **Settings**: title, text, issuer, signature, design and color.\n\n### Requirements\nGoogle Sheets, Gmail and an Apify account. Cost on Apify: about $0.005 per certificate.\n\n### How to customize\nUse `{{column}}` in the text to insert any sheet column. Designs: `certificate-classic`, `certificate-modern`, `diploma-kids`. Replace Gmail with Outlook or SMTP, or save the PDFs to Google Drive instead."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
